request.description:
Retrieve notifications for the authenticated user with filtering and pagination options.

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: notification**: Sent when a new notification is created.
  ```javascript
  socket.on('notification', (notification) => {
    console.log('New notification:', notification.message);
    displayNotification(notification);
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (React Hook):**
```typescript
import { useNotifications } from './hooks/useNotifications';
const { notifications, counts } = useNotifications(token);
useEffect(() => {
  console.log('Notifications:', notifications);
  console.log('Unread count:', counts.unread);
}, [notifications, counts]);
```

Create a new notification for a specific user.

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: notification**: Automatically sent to the target user.
  ```javascript
  socket.on('notification', (notification) => {
    console.log('New notification:', notification.message);
    updateNotificationUI(notification);
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (API Service):**
```typescript
const notificationService = new NotificationAPIService('https://api.example.com', token);
async function createNotification() {
  const notificationData = {
    userId: "user456",
    type: "alert",
    message: "Critical lab results require immediate attention",
    metadata: { labResultId: "lab123", priority: "high" }
  };
  const response = await notificationService.createNotification(notificationData);
  console.log('Notification created:', response.data);
}
```

Retrieve notification counts and statistics for the authenticated user.

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: get_notification_counts**: Client can request counts via WebSocket.
  ```javascript
  socket.emit('get_notification_counts', userId);
  socket.on('notification_counts', (counts) => {
    console.log('Notification counts:', counts);
    updateBadgeCount(counts.unread);
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (API Service):**
```typescript
const notificationService = new NotificationAPIService('https://api.example.com', token);
async function getNotificationCounts() {
  const response = await notificationService.getNotificationCounts();
  console.log('Counts:', response.data);
  updateNotificationBadge(response.data.unread);
}
```

Mark a specific notification as read.

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: mark_notification_read**: Client can mark as read via WebSocket.
  ```javascript
  socket.emit('mark_notification_read', {
    notificationId: 'notif123',
    userId: 'user456'
  });
  ```
- **Event: notification_read**: Confirmation that notification was marked as read.
  ```javascript
  socket.on('notification_read', (data) => {
    console.log('Notification marked as read:', data.id);
    updateNotificationStatus(data.id, 'read');
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (API Service):**
```typescript
const notificationService = new NotificationAPIService('https://api.example.com', token);
async function markAsRead(notificationId) {
  const response = await notificationService.markAsRead(notificationId);
  console.log('Marked as read:', response.data);
}
```

Mark all unread notifications as read for the authenticated user.

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: all_notifications_read**: Notifies that all notifications were marked as read.
  ```javascript
  socket.on('all_notifications_read', (data) => {
    console.log('All notifications marked as read for user:', data.userId);
    markAllNotificationsAsRead();
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (API Service):**
```typescript
const notificationService = new NotificationAPIService('https://api.example.com', token);
async function markAllAsRead() {
  await notificationService.markAllAsRead();
  console.log('All notifications marked as read');
  clearUnreadBadge();
}
```

Delete a specific notification (soft delete).

**WebSocket Integration:**
- **Event: notification_deleted**: Notifies that a notification was deleted.
  ```javascript
  socket.on('notification_deleted', (data) => {
    console.log('Notification deleted:', data.id);
    removeNotificationFromUI(data.id);
  });
  ```

**Frontend Example (API Service):**
```typescript
const notificationService = new NotificationAPIService('https://api.example.com', token);
async function deleteNotification(notificationId) {
  await notificationService.deleteNotification(notificationId);
  console.log('Notification deleted:', notificationId);
}
```
